Jenkins CI Pipeline — Short Command Flow
Step 1: Create Java program in GitHub
Create a public repository named simplejava.

Create a file named Simple.java and commit this code:

public class Simple {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Jenkins CI Build Successful");
    }
}



Step 2: Configure Jenkins
1. Open http://localhost:8080
2. Click New Item → enter simplejava.
3. Select Freestyle project → OK.
4. Under Source Code Management → select Git.
5. Repository URL: https://github.com/diksshita/simplejava.git
6. Branch: */main
Step 3: Configure build
Under Build Steps → Add build step → Execute Windows batch command, type:
java -version
javac Simple.java
java Simple


Click Save.
Step 4: Execute
1. Open the simplejava Jenkins job.
2. Click Build Now.
3. Open the latest build → Console Output.
Expected output
Jenkins CI Build Successful
Finished: SUCCESS
